From 9c5d8c3093d0f3b9f627c698cc1ed2d436a911c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:28:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): add guarded reserved-key recovery for
 never-created cards [daveey]

Introduce preview-default, single-card reserved-key correction with authenticated
never-existed evidence, owner and worker fences, exact local CAS, replacement-key
uniqueness, and immutable supersession receipts. Publish current corrected parent
intent before original child identities, retaining audit payloads and preventing
other-parent synthesis or compatibility downgrades. Track transient retry op IDs.
Prevent ordinary creation with detector-reserved keys without relaxing provenance.

Why: ordinary callers could create a detector-reserved key locally, then Board
correctly rejected its provenance. Existing reconciliation could neither edit that
identity nor safely retire never-created operations. A scoped audited correction
is required instead of weakening the detector or resetting rejection queues.

Proof: canonical focused suite (7 files) 880 passed; expanded recovery suite
173 passed. Broad 959-file consumer run: 17600 passed, 24 skipped, two file
timeouts; focused retry including both timeout files: 265 passed, exit 0.
Isolated exact-anchor mutation sweeps exercised custody, CAS, evidence, ordering,
creation, retry and compatibility boundaries; survivor tests added and killed.
Redundant predicates and crash-only mutants documented, not claimed assertion kills.
Read-only guard replay across 25 hub DBs: 555 reserved occurrences, exactly one
newly refused ordinary-invalid target; no detector regressions found.
New conflict, retry custody, repeat-intent, endpoint synthesis and compatibility
tests were observed RED before fixes. No production repair executed; operational
owner retains application and convergence.
